== Research

== Publications

[https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11336-024-09961-w Sufficient and Necessary Conditions for the Identifiability of DINA Models with Polytomous Responses], *Mengqi Lin* and Gongjun Xu. /Psychometrika/, 89(2), 717--740, 2024.

== Preprints

[https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.02682 Characterizing Identifiability in Boolean Factor Models], *Mengqi Lin* and Gongjun Xu. Major revision at /Journal of the American Statistical Association/.

[https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.05120 Stochastic Sensitivity Analysis for Matched Observational Studies], *Mengqi Lin*, Colin Fogarty, and Gongjun Xu. Submitted.

[https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.06601 Simultaneous Inference for False Discovery Proportions under Sensitivity Models for Observational Studies], *Mengqi Lin* and Colin Fogarty. Submitted.

== Software

- *idQ*, Python package for checking Q-matrix identifiability in cognitive diagnosis models.
- *SensitivityFDP*, Python package for simultaneous inference on false discovery proportions in observational studies under sensitivity models.
- [https://github.com/Mengqi-Lin/dbh/tree/adaptive-weights dwbh-adaptive_weights], R package for dependence-adjusted weighted Benjamini-Hochberg and general step-up procedures, with adaptive weighting.

== Talks

- /Characterizing Identifiability in Boolean Factor Models./ JSM 2026, Boston; JSM 2025, Nashville.
- /Controlling the False Discovery Proportion in Observational Studies with Hidden Bias./ ICSA 2025, Taipei; ACIC 2025, Detroit; JSM 2024, Portland.
- /Controlling the False Discovery Rate Under Dependency with the Adaptively Weighted BH Procedure./ JSM 2023, Toronto; MCP 2022, Bremen.
- /Identifiability of Cognitive Diagnosis Models with Polytomous Responses./ IMPS 2023, Washington, D.C.

